"### Functions

#### list()

> **list**(): \`string\`[]

Top-level list, distinct from \`things.list\`.

#### describe()

> **describe**(\`options\`: [\`things.ThingOptions\`](#thingsthingoptions)): \`string\`

Uses a type from a namespace.

### Namespaces

#### things

Things you can list and add.

##### Functions

###### things.list()

> **list**(\`options?\`: [\`things.ThingOptions\`](#thingsthingoptions)): \`string\`[]

List things.

###### things.add()

> **add**(\`name\`: \`string\`): \`string\`

Add a thing.

##### Type Aliases

###### things.ThingOptions

> **things.ThingOptions** = \`object\`

Options shared across things.

**Properties**

| Property | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| \`verbose?\` | \`boolean\` | Say more. |

##### Namespaces

###### things.nested

Nested even deeper.

**Functions**

**things.nested.count()**

> **count**(): \`number\`

Count nested things.

**things.nested.list()**

> **list**(): \`void\`

Has the same name as \`things.list\` and the top-level \`list\`."
