exports[`full format > sample library > matches the snapshot 1`] = `
"### Functions

#### greet()

> **greet**(\`name\`: \`string\`, \`options?\`: [\`GreetingOptions\`](#greetingoptions)): [\`GreetingResult\`](#greetingresult)

Generate a personalized greeting.

##### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| \`name\` | \`string\` | The name of the person to greet |
| \`options?\` | [\`GreetingOptions\`](#greetingoptions) | Configuration for the greeting |

##### Returns

[\`GreetingResult\`](#greetingresult)

A greeting result with the message and metadata

##### Examples

\`\`\`ts
const result = greet('World')
console.log(result.message) // "Hello, World!"
\`\`\`

\`\`\`ts
const result = greet('Professor', { formal: true })
console.log(result.message) // "Good day, Professor."
\`\`\`

#### translate()

> **translate**(\`greeting\`: [\`GreetingResult\`](#greetingresult), \`language\`: [\`Language\`](#language)): [\`GreetingResult\`](#greetingresult)

Translate a greeting to a different language.

##### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| \`greeting\` | [\`GreetingResult\`](#greetingresult) | The greeting result to translate |
| \`language\` | [\`Language\`](#language) | Target language code |

##### Returns

[\`GreetingResult\`](#greetingresult)

A new greeting result in the target language

#### hello()

> **hello**(\`name\`: \`string\`): \`string\`

Create and immediately invoke a greeting with sensible defaults.

This is the simplest way to generate a greeting — just pass a name.

##### Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| \`name\` | \`string\` | The name to greet |

##### Returns

\`string\`

The greeting message string

##### Example

\`\`\`ts
import hello from 'sample-lib'
console.log(hello('World')) // "Hello, World!"
\`\`\`

### Classes

#### GreetingGenerator

A greeting generator that maintains state.

##### Example

\`\`\`ts
const gen = new GreetingGenerator('en')
const result = gen.generate('World')
\`\`\`

##### Constructors

###### Constructor

> **new GreetingGenerator**(\`language?\`: [\`Language\`](#language)): [\`GreetingGenerator\`](#greetinggenerator)

Create a new greeting generator.

**Parameters**

| Parameter | Type | Default value | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ |
| \`language\` | [\`Language\`](#language) | \`'en'\` | The default language for greetings |

##### Methods

###### generate()

> **generate**(\`name\`: \`string\`, \`options?\`: [\`GreetingOptions\`](#greetingoptions)): [\`GreetingResult\`](#greetingresult)

Generate a greeting in the configured language.

**Parameters**

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| \`name\` | \`string\` | The name to greet |
| \`options?\` | [\`GreetingOptions\`](#greetingoptions) | Optional greeting configuration |

**Returns**

[\`GreetingResult\`](#greetingresult)

The greeting result

### Type Aliases

#### GreetingOptions

> **GreetingOptions** = \`object\`

Configuration options for the greeting system.

##### Properties

| Property | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| \`formal?\` | \`boolean\` | Whether to use formal language. |
| \`maxLength?\` | \`number\` | Maximum length of the greeting. |

#### GreetingResult

> **GreetingResult** = \`object\`

A greeting result with metadata.

##### Properties

| Property | Type | Description |
| ------ | ------ | ------ |
| \`message\` | \`string\` | The formatted greeting message. |
| \`timestamp\` | \`Date\` | Timestamp when the greeting was generated. |

#### Language

> **Language** = \`"en"\` \\| \`"es"\` \\| \`"fr"\` \\| \`"ja"\`

Supported greeting languages.

### Variables

#### MAX\\_GREETING\\_LENGTH

> \`const\` **MAX\\_GREETING\\_LENGTH**: \`100\` = \`100\`

Default maximum greeting length."
`;
